  "implemented_scope": [
    "Intersect and Subtract operate on exactly two filled sibling shapes. Geometry sections are united within each operand before the operation; curves, holes and transformations survive public-only VSDX reopen. Empty/degenerate results refuse without mutation. Existing Union source/behavior/protection/reference/identity and geometry budgets remain authoritative.",
    "Subtraction requires an explicit base choice because canvas selection is unordered. Distinct native menu items retain UUID identities even with duplicate labels. Owner/state/revision/page/raw-selection/IME/cancel/close gates lead into the existing owned asynchronous calculation and one-step undo transaction.",
    "All Boolean results use the first operand in document order for appearance, become topmost within their containing Shapes owner and remain selected. These are explicit local policies, not first-selected/reference parity.",
    "PNG Page preserves physical paper clipping and prior pixel dimensions. Content includes printable foreground and assigned backgrounds, including off-page artwork. Selection expands selected groups and group-owned edges without editability filtering; only selected foreground determines the crop, while assigned backgrounds remain painted within it.",
    "Cropped PNG measures conservative physical paint bounds from prepared paths/strokes/images/text, complete frozen connector routes, arrows and labels. It aligns outward to the raster grid with one full pixel guard per side; exact pixel dimensions avoid floating-point floor loss. Two bounded main passes feed immutable worker assembly.",
    "Native export settles text/page interaction before snapshot capture, refuses pending composition/calculation, and binds selection drafts to raw UUID sets as well as immutable owner/state/revision/page identity. Submitted jobs retain normal captured-snapshot semantics. Unsupported images refuse cropped modes while Page retains the prior placeholder."
  ],
